Technical Source Audit — Pdf-Hub (DocCraft)
Context
DocCraft is a React 19 + TypeScript 6 SPA PDF editor (pnpm monorepo, Vite 8, Zustand 5, PDF.js 5, Konva 10, Tesseract.js 7). The audit covers the frontend source (frontend/src/, 358 TS/TSX files, 2.7 MB) plus build/CI configuration. The goal is to surface confirmed bugs, security gaps, tech debt, and test coverage holes — with file:line precision so each finding is immediately actionable.
Findings by Severity
CRITICAL — Confirmed Bugs
C1 · Resource leak in PDF page-load loop
File: frontend/src/components/workspace/DocumentWorkspace.tsx:153–162
The for (let i = 1; i <= doc.numPages; i++) loop that builds the search index runs without checking cancelled. If the component unmounts (user navigates away or opens a different PDF), the loop continues loading every remaining page — allocating PageProxy objects and building index entries that are immediately discarded. On a 500-page document this can OOM the browser.
Fix: add if (cancelled) break; as the first statement inside the loop body.
C2 · JSON.parse() without try/catch on persisted table data
File: frontend/src/components/writer/WriterElementNode.tsx:257
JSON.parse(element.content || '{"headers":[],"rows":[]}') is called inline inside JSX with no error boundary or try/catch. If a table element's content field is corrupted in IndexedDB (partial write, version mismatch, manual edit), this throws synchronously inside a render, crashing the entire writer overlay with an unhandled exception. writerDisplayHtml.ts (writer-v2) already wraps its parse in try/catch correctly — the v1 writer path does not.
Fix: wrap in try/catch, fall back to {"headers":[],"rows":[]} and log via the structured logger.
C3 · Silent data loss on annotation autosave failure
Files: DocumentWorkspace.tsx:198 (debounced save), DocumentWorkspace.tsx:210 (pagehide flush)
Both call void saveAnnotations(...) — discarding the promise. If IndexedDB is locked, quota-exceeded, or in a private-browsing context, the rejection is swallowed. No toast, no log, no retry.
Fix: attach .catch(err => logError('annotations-save-failed', { err })) to both calls. The pagehide path can't use await but can fire a synchronous log.
HIGH — Security Gaps
H1 · dangerouslySetInnerHTML on unsanitized element.content (v1 writer)
File: frontend/src/components/writer/WriterElementNode.tsx:246
<div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: element.content || '...' }} /> for type === 'rich-text' elements. The v1 writer's RichTextEditorPanel calls sanitizeHtml() before storing content, but: (a) sanitizeHtml() allows the style attribute unconditionally, which permits CSS expression() in legacy IE and url('javascript:...') in some parsers; (b) any code path that writes to element.content without going through the sanitizer (e.g., clipboard paste fallback, direct store mutation in tests, import from project ZIP) bypasses this protection entirely.
The v2 writer (WriterRichElementBox, writerDisplayHtml.ts) correctly escapes all text nodes and never injects raw HTML from storage — v1 has the gap.
Fix: (a) strip style from the ALLOWED_ATTRIBUTES set in htmlSanitizer.ts or add CSS sanitization; (b) call sanitizeHtml() at render time in WriterElementNode rather than relying on call-site discipline.
H2 · style attribute and data: URIs allowed in HTML sanitizer
File: frontend/src/core/writer/htmlSanitizer.ts:19–21, 83–89
ALLOWED_ATTRIBUTES includes style. The href/src guard blocks javascript:, vbscript:, and data:text/html but not data:application/xhtml+xml or data:text/svg+xml (both can execute script in some browsers). style attributes can carry background: url(...) with same-origin cookie-stealing requests in server environments.
Severity in this app is reduced because it's a SPA with no auth cookies, but the sanitizer is also used by clipboard paste paths where content is external.
Fix: remove style from ALLOWED_ATTRIBUTES or run CSS through a second sanitization pass; extend the data: blocklist.
MEDIUM — State & Correctness
M1 · 4× setState inside useEffect body (documented, unfixed)
Files/lines: documented in knownissues.md §ESLint Errors 1–4
SelectBoxCopyResultPanel.tsx:48 — derive from props via useMemo instead
ColorPickerPopover.tsx:25 — remove effect, use controlled prop
DocumentWorkspace.tsx:183 — move setRestoredCount(0) inside the loadStored async function (after await)
WriterElementBox.tsx:46 — use useLayoutEffect or derive from props
These cause extra render cycles. The DocumentWorkspace case is worst: the synchronous setRestoredCount(0) fires a render before the async load finishes, meaning the restored-annotation count briefly shows zero even when annotations exist.
M2 · Annotation filter creates new arrays every render
File: DocumentWorkspace.tsx:340–344
pageAnnotations={annotations.filter(...).filter(...).slice().sort(...)} runs on every render of the parent, producing a new array reference each time. PageSurface is not memoized, so it re-renders on every annotation-unrelated state change (zoom, tool switch, panning). On a 100-page document in continuous-scroll mode, this creates 100× unnecessary re-renders.
Fix: extract pageAnnotations into a useMemo keyed on [annotations, pageNumber, hideResolved]; wrap PageSurface with React.memo.
M3 · Missing useMemo dependencies in WriterPopupEditor
File: frontend/src/components/writer-v2/WriterPopupEditor.tsx:79
Documented in knownissues.md. element.editorStateJson and element.plainText are missing from the useMemo dep array. The editor initializes from a stale snapshot when the element is programmatically updated (e.g., via macro).
M4 · Deprecated document.execCommand() in v1 rich-text editor
File: frontend/src/components/writer/RichTextEditorPanel.tsx:111, 158, 186
execCommand('insertHTML', ...) is removed from the HTML spec and already deprecated in Chrome/Firefox. The v2 writer uses Lexical properly. The v1 path will silently break when browsers remove support.
Fix: migrate to Selection.getRangeAt(0) + Range.insertNode(), or flag the v1 writer as fully superseded by v2.
LOW — Tech Debt
L1 · Monolithic components
DocumentWorkspace.tsx: 2,124 lines. Mixes PDF loading, search indexing, annotation CRUD, autosave, viewport fitting, IntersectionObserver page tracking, panning, and render logic. No error boundary wraps the component.
MacrosSidebar.tsx: 1,643 lines.
Neither is immediately broken but both are hard to test in isolation and cause wide-blast re-renders.
Recommendation: split DocumentWorkspace into PdfLoader (hook), AnnotationAutosave (hook), PageScroller (component), and keep render logic thin.
L2 · 4× non-component exports breaking React Fast Refresh (documented, unfixed)
Files: InspectorPanel.tsx:747, MacroNestedBranchEditor.tsx:236, Tabs.tsx:9, WriterOverlayLayer.tsx:145
These disable HMR for those files, degrading DX. Fix: extract to separate *Utils.ts / *Context.ts files.
L3 · Missing eslint-plugin-react (documented, unfixed)
Causes the react/no-danger rule in WriterRichElementBox.tsx to be an unknown rule, suppressing the intended warning about dangerouslySetInnerHTML.
Fix: pnpm add -D eslint-plugin-react and register in eslint.config.js.
L4 · CI Node version inconsistency
deploy.yml uses Node 20; certify-writer-overlay-v2.yml uses Node 22. Different V8 engine behaviors (especially around Intl, crypto) could mask environment-specific bugs.
Fix: pin to one LTS version across all workflow files.
Test Coverage Gaps
T1 · annotations/store.ts (627 lines, 30+ Zustand actions) — no dedicated unit tests
This store is the core of the annotation system. Bugs here (wrong updateManyAnnotations merge, off-by-one in setActiveAnnotationId, wrong selection toggle) are invisible until a full UI integration test. The DocumentWorkspace.test.tsx tests restore/save but not individual CRUD actions.
T2 · PdfEditAdapter.ts (828 lines) — no error-path tests
Functions like removePage, reorderPages, mergePdfs have no tests for invalid inputs (remove the only page, empty merge list, corrupted bytes). These guard user operations with real destructive consequences.
T3 · content-ops.ts (macro content step, 673 lines) — existing slice test covers happy paths only
content-ops.slice3.test.ts exists but the HTML sanitization and table-import paths have no adversarial tests (malformed HTML, deeply nested tables, <script> injection via paste).
